<title>TURKEY: Turkey sets 9-month bond auction for Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets 9-month bond auction for Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish central bank said the Treasury would auction on Tuesday nine-month bonds after it sold 75.73 trillion lira nominal-valued six-month bills on June 24.</p>
<p>    Maturity    : April 1, 1998.</p>
<p>    Amount	: -</p>
<p>    Coupon	: -</p>
<p>Auction date: July 1, 1997</p>
<p>Value date  : July 2, 1997</p>
<p>The treasury faces about 21.3 trillion lira of coupon repayments on July 2, Wednesday as three-month interest maturing on 109.8 trillion lira worth two-year inflation-indexed bonds it issued on April 1.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
